; 40-latex.kurt

; `latex SYMBOL REPLACEMENT` tells Kurt how to render a symbol when producing
; a LaTeX proof document -- run `kurt -l my-proof.kurt` on the command line
; to generate one.  `src/kurt/theories/latex.kurt` already maps most builtins
; (`implies` to `\Rightarrow`, `∀` to `\forall`, `not`/`¬` to `\lnot`, ...);
; you only need `latex` yourself for symbols you introduce.

infix "xor" 15 15
latex "xor" "\oplus"

bool A, B
use A xor B
A xor B

; This mapping only affects `-l` output (or `format latex`, which switches
; the session's own print format to LaTeX) -- it changes nothing about
; proving or checking, it is purely cosmetic, exactly like `alias`
; (37-alias.kurt) is purely syntactic.
